bout the fastdl.app downloader. If you can't find the answer to your questi=
on, feel free to ask through email on our contact page.</p><ul><li itemscop=
e=3D"" itemprop=3D"mainEntity" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Question"><h3=
 itemprop=3D"name" _msttexthash=3D"563264" _msthash=3D"93">What exactly is =
FastDl.app?</h3><div itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"acceptedAnswer" itemtype=3D=
"https://schema.org/Answer"><div itemprop=3D"text" _msttexthash=3D"30623918=
" _msthash=3D"94">FastDl.app is a browser-based helper that lets you save p=
ublic Instagram content - videos, photos, Reels, Stories, IGTV and carousel=
s - to your own device for offline viewing. It works straight from the webs=
ite; no software install is required.</div></div></li><li itemscope=3D"" it=
emprop=3D"mainEntity" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Question"><h3 itemprop=
=3D"name" _msttexthash=3D"960895" _msthash=3D"95">Is downloading from Insta=
gram legal?</h3><div itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"acceptedAnswer" itemtype=3D=
"https://schema.org/Answer"><div itemprop=3D"text" _msttexthash=3D"35312849=
" _msthash=3D"96">Saving public posts for personal use is generally allowed=
, but copyright always belongs to the creator. Please keep the files privat=
e unless you have the owner=E2=80=99s permission to share or reuse them.</d=
iv></div></li><li itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"mainEntity" itemtype=3D"https:=
//schema.org/Question"><h3 itemprop=3D"name" _msttexthash=3D"994487" _mstha=
sh=3D"97">What formats and quality do you offer?</h3><div itemscope=3D"" it=
emprop=3D"acceptedAnswer" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Answer"><div itemp=
rop=3D"text" _msttexthash=3D"20847216" _msthash=3D"98">Photos arrive as JPG=
 (up to 1080 =C3=97 1350 px - the platform=E2=80=99s own limit). Videos sav=
e as MP4, typically in HD 720p if the source was uploaded in that quality. =
No watermarks are added.</div></div></li><li itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"mai=
nEntity" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Question"><h3 itemprop=3D"name" _ms=
ttexthash=3D"970138" _msthash=3D"99">Do I need to log in or create an accou=
nt?</h3><div itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"acceptedAnswer" itemtype=3D"https:/=
/schema.org/Answer"><div itemprop=3D"text" _msttexthash=3D"13684957" _mstha=
sh=3D"100">No. Just paste the Instagram link - there=E2=80=99s no registrat=
ion, no Instagram credentials, and no cookies that track you across the web=
.</div></div></li><li itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"mainEntity" itemtype=3D"ht=
tps://schema.org/Question"><h3 itemprop=3D"name" _msttexthash=3D"1095965" _=
msthash=3D"101">Are there any limits on daily downloads?</h3><div itemscope=
=3D"" itemprop=3D"acceptedAnswer" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Answer"><d=
iv itemprop=3D"text" _msttexthash=3D"9067864" _msthash=3D"102">None at all.=
 Download one item or a hundred - our servers don=E2=80=99t impose caps.</d=
iv></div></li><li itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"mainEntity" itemtype=3D"https:=
//schema.org/Question"><h3 itemprop=3D"name" _msttexthash=3D"441844" _mstha=
sh=3D"103">How do I download a post?</h3><div itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"ac=
ceptedAnswer" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Answer"><ol itemprop=3D"text">=
<li><p _msttexthash=3D"1160419" _msthash=3D"104">Copy the link to the Insta=
gram post or Reel</p></li><li><p _msttexthash=3D"2405312" _msthash=3D"105">=
Go to FastDl.app, paste the link into the field, and hit Download</p></li><=
li><p _msttexthash=3D"2124174" _msthash=3D"106">Pick the quality you want; =
the file is delivered instantly</p></li></ol></div></li><li itemscope=3D"" =
itemprop=3D"mainEntity" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Question"><h3 itempr=
op=3D"name" _msttexthash=3D"1150006" _msthash=3D"107">Can I grab content fr=
om private accounts?</h3><div itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"acceptedAnswer" it=
emtype=3D"https://schema.org/Answer"><div itemprop=3D"text" _msttexthash=3D=
"34657064" _msthash=3D"108">Sorry, no. We respect user privacy, so only pub=
lic posts are accessible. If you can=E2=80=99t view the post in a logged-ou=
t browser tab, FastDl.app can=E2=80=99t fetch it either.</div></div></li><l=
i itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"mainEntity" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Que=
stion"><h3 itemprop=3D"name" _msttexthash=3D"1216605" _msthash=3D"109">Whic=
h devices and browsers are supported?</h3><div itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"a=
cceptedAnswer" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Answer"><div itemprop=3D"text=
" _msttexthash=3D"14142700" _msthash=3D"110">Any modern browser on Windows,=
 macOS, Linux, Android, iOS or even ChromeOS. Tested in Chrome, Safari, Fir=
efox, Edge, Opera and Brave - both desktop and mobile versions.</div></div>=
</li><li itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"mainEntity" itemtype=3D"https://schema.=
org/Question"><h3 itemprop=3D"name" _msttexthash=3D"1283659" _msthash=3D"11=
1">Where do the files go on my phone or computer?</h3><div itemscope=3D"" i=
temprop=3D"acceptedAnswer" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Answer"><div item=
prop=3D"text" _msttexthash=3D"59771296" _msthash=3D"112">On desktop they la=
nd in your default =E2=80=9CDownloads=E2=80=9D folder. On mobile you can fi=
nd them in the browser=E2=80=99s downloads list or the =E2=80=9CFiles=E2=80=
=9D app. Most gallery apps will index them automatically.</div></div></li><=
li itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"mainEntity" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Qu=
estion"><h3 itemprop=3D"name" _msttexthash=3D"1189578" _msthash=3D"113">Is =
my link history stored on your servers?</h3><div itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D=
"acceptedAnswer" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Answer"><div itemprop=3D"te=
xt" _msttexthash=3D"12905243" _msthash=3D"114">No. Links are processed in r=
eal time; once the download link is generated and delivered, both the origi=
nal URL and the converted file are wiped from our cache.</div></div></li><l=
i itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"mainEntity" itemtype=3D"https://schema.org/Que=
stion"><h3 itemprop=3D"name" _msttexthash=3D"481923" _msthash=3D"115">Why m=
ight the speed drop?</h3><div itemscope=3D"" itemprop=3D"acceptedAnswer" it=
emtype=3D"https://schema.org/Answer"><div itemprop=3D"text" _msttexthash=3D=
"28629536" _msthash=3D"116">A slow network, heavy ISP throttling or Instagr=
am rate-limits can reduce throughput. Switching to another Wi-Fi, disabling=
 a VPN, or trying a different browser usually fixes it. If not, reach out t=
hrough the contact page - we answer fast.</div></div></li></ul></section>


